# Udev rules for ASUS Aura Sync Hardware on Linux
# Target: ASUS ROG Strix GeForce GTX 1060 & ROG STRIX Z270E GAMING

# 1. Allow group 'i2c' read/write access to NVIDIA GPU I2C character device
KERNEL=="i2c-[0-9]*", GROUP="i2c", MODE="0660"

# 2. Daily non-root usage options:
# Option A (Recommended): Allow passwordless sudo for the aura-ctl binary:
#   echo "%wheel ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /home/alexkala/repos/asus-aura-controller/aura-ctl" | sudo tee /etc/sudoers.d/99-aura-ctl
#
# Option B (File capabilities for raw I/O port access on NCT6793D):
#   sudo setcap cap_sys_rawio+ep $(readlink -f $(which python3))
